/*  FUNCTION NAME:      PLAYERTURNS
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Builds the array of which player owns each turn, given a per-turn "pass to next player" flag. Supports any number of players and any starting player.*/
/*  RETURNS:            array: the player who owns each turn, one per advance flag
    PARAMETERS:
        advance         (Required) 1-D boolean, one per turn. TRUE = play moves to the next player AFTER this turn (i.e. the current player did not earn another go). A go-again trigger is just NOT(...).
        players         (Optional) Player labels in turn order. Default {1;2}. Any length gives N-player support.
        start           (Optional) The starting player. A number is a 1-based index into players; a text value is matched against players as a label (so start = "B" begins on player B). With numeric player labels, start is always an index — pass the label's position. Default 1.
    EXAMPLE:            =PLAYERTURNS({TRUE;TRUE;TRUE;TRUE;TRUE}, {"A";"B";"C"}) -> {A;B;C;A;B}
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-07-01  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-07-01  Claude      Live in loops/ next to SCANLEAD (no cross-library dependency resolution). Inline the +1 circular rotation (MOD(cur, nP) + 1) to drop the CIRCPOS/math dependency — PLAYERTURNS is now self-contained in loops.
                        2026-07-01  Claude      start accepts a player label (text) as well as a 1-based index (number); type decides, so numeric player labels keep pure index semantics.
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
PLAYERTURNS = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [advance],
    [players],
    [start],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        ps, TOCOL(IF(ISOMITTED(players), {1;2}, players)),
        nP, ROWS(ps),
        s0, IF(ISOMITTED(start), 1, IF(ISTEXT(start), XMATCH(start, ps), start)),
        idx, SCANLEAD(s0, advance, LAMBDA(cur, a, IF(a, MOD(cur, nP) + 1, cur))),
        result, INDEX(ps, idx),
        result
)
);
